        "original_id": "72dd3d11-ac52-552f-b686-8fe06e7c5aae",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Spirit Airlines\n- Places: Miramar, Florida; Atlantic City; Chicago–O'Hare; Dallas/Fort Worth; Detroit; Fort Lauderdale; Las Vegas; Detroit Metropolitan Wayne County Airport; Romulus, Michigan; Detroit\n- Topics: Ultra low-cost carriers; airport identifiers\n\nFacts:\n- Spirit Airlines, Inc. is an American ultra low-cost carrier headquartered in Miramar, Florida.\n- As of 2015, Spirit Airlines operated bases at Atlantic City, Chicago–O'Hare, Dallas/Fort Worth, Detroit, Fort Lauderdale, and Las Vegas.\n- Detroit Metropolitan Wayne County Airport is a major international airport in the United States.\n- Detroit Metropolitan Wayne County Airport covers 4,850 acres in Romulus, Michigan, a suburb of Detroit.\n- Detroit Metropolitan Wayne County Airport is usually called Detroit Metro Airport, Metro Airport, or DTW.\n- Detroit Metropolitan Wayne County Airport has the identifiers IATA DTW, ICAO KDTW, and FAA LID DTW.",
